      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely not, you must never give aspirin to a child under 12 because it can cause Reye's syndrome, a dangerous condition that can be fatal. Instead, you should immediately give him a dose of acetaminophen (Tylenol) or ibuprofen (Advil) at the correct weight-based dosage found on the bottle. If he has a high fever, you can also use a warm bath to help lower his temperature while you wait for the medicine to work.",
